aces-survey 0.1.0: survey and photogrammetry on ACES OS

Stack
  Plan     QGIS (Arch extra) + the FlyPath plugin (vendored; aces-survey-setup installs it per user): draw the survey
           area, set altitude and overlap, export a DJI WPML KMZ for the DJI Fly app. 2D grid, corridor and orbit
           missions, terrain follow, cross-hatch, battery splitting; semi-automatic (timed shot) or full-automatic
           (one waypoint per photo) capture.
  Fly      DJI Fly on the RC 2 or a phone. Consumer DJI aircraft (Mini 5 Pro, Mavic 4 Pro, Flip, Neo, Lito) have no
           Mobile SDK (DJI "Product SDK Compatibility", read 2026-10-09), so no third-party app can fly them; the
           aircraft's own waypoint engine flies the KMZ instead.
  Process  WebODM (webodm.org, AGPL-3.0) with the ODX engine (AGPL-3.0): orthomosaic, DSM/DTM, point cloud, textured
           mesh, Gaussian splats, ground control points. aces-webodm runs the pinned stack under Docker; the GPU node
           (webodm/nodeodx:gpu) is used when nvidia-container-toolkit is installed.
  Deliver  QGIS (contours, cut-and-fill volumes, map layouts) and CloudCompare (AUR package cloudcompare, optional) for
           point-cloud cleaning, cloud-to-cloud comparison and volumes.

Loading a mission into DJI Fly (the app has no import button)
  1. In DJI Fly create any small waypoint mission and save it; note the name it gets (Waypoint_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS).
  2. Export the FlyPath KMZ and rename it to exactly that name.
  3. Copy it over the dummy file:
       RC 2 or Android phone:  Android/data/dji.go.v5/files/waypoint/  (USB file transfer; older installs use dji.go.v2)
       iPhone:                 Files app > On My iPhone > DJI Fly > files > waypoint
     The thumbnail in the app does not refresh; the route does.
  4. Open DJI Fly > Waypoint > My Routes, check the route and the speed (the app sometimes resets the speed from the
     KMZ), then fly.

Camera for mapping (Mini 5 Pro)
  50 MP, 4:3 (the full 8192x6144 frame, never 16:9), JPEG, a fixed shutter of 1/1000 s or faster with auto ISO, gimbal
  set by the mission (-90 degrees). Semi-automatic capture uses the timed-shot interval; check the minimum interval
  at 50 MP in your firmware before planning the speed, or use full-automatic capture. No RTK on the Mini series:
  expect 1 to 3 m absolute error without ground control; tag GCPs in WebODM for survey-grade work.

Commands
  aces-survey-setup [--remove]   install FlyPath into the QGIS profile and create the WebODM tree (per user).
                                 If the FlyPath menu is missing after the very first QGIS start, tick it once under
                                 Plugins > Manage and Install Plugins > Installed; QGIS then keeps it enabled.
  aces-webodm start|stop|status|open|update|logs|path
  aces-console webodm            open the console URL from the aces configuration (server.webodm)

Policy
  The stack processes imagery the operator captured or is authorised to process. Imagery of other people's property
  and of controlled sites follows the project class and the end-use gate (aces policy show). Flight rules are the
  pilot's responsibility (CASA for Australia: registration and accreditation for any commercial flight, whatever the
  aircraft weighs).
